  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LSU 2022, Capacity development Stockholm+50</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">LSU 2022, Kapacitetsst&#xe4;rkande Stockholm+50</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsens &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att st&#xf6;da unga fr&#xe5;n l&#xe5;g- och medelinkomstl&#xe4;nder att delta i diskussionerna inf&#xf6;r, under och efter Stockholm+50, samt att st&#xe4;rka ungas kapacitet och kunskap f&#xf6;r att kunna ta en st&#xf6;rre plats i framtida internationella dialoger om globala fr&#xe5;gor. Insatsen g&#xf6;rs i samarbete mellan LSU och Stockholm+50 Youth Task Force.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contributions overarching goal is to support Low- to middle income country (LMIC) youth in participating in discussions leading up to, during and after Stockholm+50, as well as strengthening LMIC youth capacity and knowledge to be able to take a more central role in future international dialogues on global issues. The contribution is a collaboration between LSU and the Stockholm+50 Youth Task Force.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention aims to enhance and enable the meaningfully and equal participation by youth from low- and middle income countries (LMIC) in the processes for engagement leading up to, during and after the Stockholm50 conference in Stockholm in 2nd-3rd of June 2022. The intervention is looking to support LMIC youth in increasing their capabilities to paticipate in an meaningful way by hosting consultations leading up to the conference, as well as directly enabling the participation of LMIC youth at the conference itself and in side events. 

LSU with partners is also looking to ensure the retention and advancement of LMIC youth&apos;s needs, ideas and demands in the aftermath of Stockholm50 based on the supported modes of engagement. They will also seek to strengthen the capacity and understanding between youth actors and decision makers in how to create meaningful youth participation in multilateral dialogues and conferences.</narrative>
  </description>
